  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program for Income Generation through Urban and Semi-urban Self-Employment Aimed at Victims of the Armed Conflict in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to serve the victim population prioritized by the Ministry of Labor and the Victims Unit who are in different stages of the program for income generation through urban and semi-urban self-employment. This program has a focus and call phase, the second phase includes a virtual training process on basic business topics, a third phase in which the development of the business plan is developed, a fourth phase that focuses on the delivery of assets and a fifth phase that focuses on monitoring and support. The program will be implemented virtually, except for asset deliveries. Participants are divided into three groups, depending on the phase of the program they are in; The first group requires total attention to the route, the second group begins with the validation of the business plan and deliveries and the third group only requires the assistance and training process on commercial issues for the business units they already have, to The first two groups must deliver elements to the business units.</narrative>
  </description>
